      "id": "db2a520eeb1c-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word) Candle : Melt :: Camphor : ?",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word)</p><p>Candle : Melt :: Camphor : ? </p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Condense",
          "html": "Condense"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Evaporate",
          "html": "Evaporate"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Sublimate",
          "html": "Sublimate"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Freeze",
          "html": "Freeze"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>A candle melts when heated. It means \"melt\" is the action that happens to a candle under heat.</p><p>Camphor is a solid that directly transforms into a gas when heated, without going through a liquid phase, which is the process of sublimation. </p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
